      "title": "Sydney man charged after alleged gunfire prompted Dulwich Hill lockdown",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/19/man-charged-dulwich-hill-sydney-inner-west-alleged-gun-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Police responding to reports of an alleged stolen car in Dulwich Hill were told a man was armed with a firearm</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>An alleged gunman with “shaggy hair” has been arrested following reports of a confrontation about an allegedly stolen car which was set on fire prompting him to flee the scene.</p><p>The 32-year-old man was arrested late Sunday in Sydney’s inner west, after being on the run since Friday morning, following an appeal by the police.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/19/man-charged-dulwich-hill-sydney-inner-west-alleged-gun-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
